  "tree": {
   "definition": "residue-group fold G = w: each peer folds its own M_k microbatches locally in fp32 and sends one fp32 partial per unit piece to its owner, released as the last W produces the unit (forward emission); owners add w-1 partials; gathers after; nothing streams before the last W",
   "arms": [
    "interior_w4.tree (F5 primary)",
    "stage0.tree"
   ]
  },
  "stage0_padding": "per peer q, its i-th owned microbatch (global index i*w + q, i = 0 .. M/w - 1) occupies the slot [i*tau, (i+1)*tau), tau = C_B'/(M/w); with cF, cB, cW = c_s times the pinned op split: F runs [i*tau, i*tau + cF], B runs [(i+1)*tau - cW - cB, (i+1)*tau - cW], W runs [(i+1)*tau - cW, (i+1)*tau] (the idle between F and B is the wait for the downstream backward); no F runs ahead of its slot. So the last W ends at C_B', the period is C_B', window_s = 0, and step t+1's first F is due at C_B'. A harness may realize it with a per-peer wait of tau - c_s between each F and its B (one stand-in per peer, never one shared by the peers, comm 0, no exchange), as long as the op times above result.",
  "exposure_definition": "E = how late step t+1's forward is, units in forward order (D accumulates), against the peer's compute end, from ONE simulation of every microbatch's traffic (SCHEDULER-I17); every E4 arm has window_s = 0, so E is the exposure beyond the slot",
  "host_dram": "a resource in the simulation at k 10 per side (I17), unconstrained here: every peer runs on one Mac whose DRAM (~100 GB/s) carries <= 2.7 GB/s of exchange passes; the shim does not pace it",
  "embed_unit": "one fp32 unit (tok + pos, I17), released when W(mb) starts; stride and LPT own its two tensors whole (tok and pos may sit on different peers)",
  "fold_rule": "left fold of every microbatch's contribution in canonical order, each at the measured rate ((b_g + 16) B/element for a 2-byte wire, 12 B for fp32), then AdamW at 30 B/element; the unit's gathers leave after the last fold and the AdamW (I17)",
  "today_mode": "whole-stage flush: stride ZeRO-1 of whole tensors (params[k::w], stage 0 base 2, 12 parameters per block, modules at +2, +4, +8, +10; tok and pos are tensors 0 and 1), fp32 wire (b_g = b_p = 4 on every unit, so folds at 12 B/element), every unit's gradient pieces of W(mb) released at W(mb)'s END (the Embed too, not at W start); the emission order is therefore irrelevant; queues, chunks, resources, latencies and the left fold as I17; full step barrier: every gather released at Tb = max over (unit, owner) of (its last fold + AdamW), and step t+1's F on every unit waits for Tb and for that unit's gather; boundary bytes as every other arm"
 },
