   "id": "SC-4 / SPEC SCHEDULER-I17",
   "date": "2026-10-10",
   "reason": "The granted derivation (r6_e4.py on round 4's exch4) let a hot owner's gather egress overlap its own gradient ingress (derivation.md section 2's V_max/cap term) and modelled no host DRAM, no left fold of every contribution, and no whole-stage flush. SCHEDULER-I17, the SPEC of record, releases a unit's gathers only after the owner's last fold and AdamW, puts host DRAM in the simulation, and reads E from one simulation of every microbatch. Re-derived by an independent oracle written from the SPEC text; every input the granted PLAN pins is kept. The stage-0 padding is placed per microbatch (window_s 0) and the 'today' arms get a whole-stage-flush mode (scaled.stage0_padding, scaled.today_mode).",
